INSERT INTO Impulse_Digital_X_site_content (`id`, `type`, `contentType`, `pagetitle`, `longtitle`, `description`, `alias`, `link_attributes`, `published`, `pub_date`, `unpub_date`, `parent`, `isfolder`, `introtext`, `content`, `richtext`, `template`, `menuindex`, `searchable`, `cacheable`, `createdby`, `createdon`, `editedby`, `editedon`, `deleted`, `deletedon`, `deletedby`, `publishedon`, `publishedby`, `menutitle`, `donthit`, `privateweb`, `privatemgr`, `content_dispo`, `hidemenu`, `class_key`, `context_key`, `content_type`, `uri`, `uri_override`, `hide_children_in_tree`, `show_in_tree`, `properties`, `alias_visible`) VALUES (1044, 'document', 'text/html', 'Micropigmentation prices in Bucharest', 'Micropigmentation & brow tattoo prices in Bucharest 2026 | LBar', 'Permanent makeup prices in Bucharest at LBar ⭐ Brows, lips, eyeliner. From 280 RON with a custom shape ⚡ Lasts up to 2 years ☝100% natural look. TOP Masters', 'prices', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, '', '', 1, 14, 6, 1, 1, 1, UNIX_TIMESTAMP(), 1, UNIX_TIMESTAMP(), 0, 0, 0, UNIX_TIMESTAMP(), 1, 'Prices', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'modDocument', 'en', 1, 'prices', 0, 0, 1, '{\"ms2gallery\":{\"media_source\":\"2\"}}', 1);
INSERT INTO Impulse_Digital_X_site_tmplvar_contentvalues (tmplvarid, contentid, value) VALUES
  (67, 1044, 'Is the price of permanent makeup justified?'),
  (68, 1044, '<p>Naturally, when you see the cost of a cosmetic tattoo, you might wonder: “Why this price?” You have probably already come across artists who charge several times less, or even significantly more. The price of a tattoo procedure covers a whole range of essential costs that the studio has to invest every month in order to offer quality services. Here is how the cost of permanent makeup is made up.</p>'),
  (69, 1044, '<h2>What the price of a micropigmentation procedure includes</h2>\r\n<p>In any business, the final price of a product or service may include a number of costs of various kinds. So whenever a consumable is used for you during a procedure, keep in mind that we bought it to have it on hand for you and provided it at no extra charge. So what exactly is included in the price?</p>\r\n<h3>Quality of the result</h3>\r\n<p>Of course, what matters most to every client is the quality of the result and the safety of their health. A good result reflects the skilled work of a professional artist. This is where their experience comes in: understanding and assessing the procedure for a specific area and applying the right technique. Knowing how to do a tattoo is not enough. It is essential to understand which color type suits the makeup being applied and how it will look on a particular skin type. So it is important to be able to predict the result in advance, so that it turns out perfect. Clearly, all of this comes with experience. <br />And experience is built not only through constant practice, but also through continuous professional development: attending masterclasses and industry events, studying ever more advanced materials and equipment, and so on. Development takes investment and money, and the artist expects it to pay off in the future. That is why, above all, you are paying to be sure of a safe, effective, high-quality result.</p>\r\n<h3>The cost of consumables</h3>\r\n<p>All consumables, purchased individually for each client, are included in the price of permanent makeup. These include not only pigments and single-use needles, but also dry and wet wipes, cotton swabs and cotton pads, disposable caps and shoe covers, masks, sheets, disinfectants and many other items. The price also covers the extras clients can enjoy at the studio: hygiene products, sweets and more.</p>\r\n<h3>The cost of equipment</h3>\r\n<p>High-quality professional equipment that won\'t let you down mid-procedure usually costs a great deal of money. Part of the cost of recouping it is also included in the price of the tattoo.</p>\r\n<h3>Studio maintenance costs</h3>\r\n<p>To make sure you feel comfortable at our studio, we have invested significant sums in fitting it out. The price of a micropigmentation procedure covers not only the costs we have already incurred, but also those we have to cover every month, such as utility bills.</p>\r\n<h3>Staff salaries</h3>\r\n<p>We want not only our clients to be happy with the result, but also our team to be happy with their work. That is why we pay every employee a competitive, decent salary. In fact, this is also what motivates us to deliver the quality of service you expect.</p>\r\n<h3>Why are prices much lower at other studios?</h3>\r\n<p>Obviously, a lower price means the artist has saved money on certain materials. This is quite risky, because cutting corners on the quality of consumables, disinfection equipment and products, and micropigmentation equipment can lower the level of safety for your health. It can also leave you with a terrible tattoo that will disappoint you, to say the least. Low prices for micropigmentation are often charged by beginner artists who don\'t yet have enough experience. It is up to you to decide whether you are willing to entrust your face to a novice, or whether it is worth paying more for this service and being 100% sure of the perfect result you wanted.</p>\r\n<h3>Does a higher price mean a better result?</h3>\r\n<p>While a low price for permanent makeup signals cost-cutting, an excessively high price indicates that the studio owner simply wants to earn more. That is the whole secret.</p>\r\n<p>Don\'t skimp on your tattoo.<br />But don\'t overpay either: protect your budget. Trust only professional artists who can make your dream come true with quality work that never puts your health or beauty at risk.</p>'),
  (70, 1044, 'seo-img-1.jpg'),
  (93, 1044, '<p>Our LBar permanent makeup studio in Bucharest has two levels of artists: TOP Master and TOP Trainer. The difference lies in their experience and the number of procedures they have performed, and this is exactly what determines the price of your tattoo. Rest assured that whichever artist you choose, the result will exceed your expectations. After all, LBar works first and foremost for quality and to delight you with beautiful permanent makeup.</p>'),
  (132, 1044, 'Price list: eyebrow micropigmentation'),
  (134, 1044, '[{\"MIGX_id\":\"1\",\"col-1\":\"Powder brows micropigmentation\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"6\",\"col-1\":\"Microblading brows\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min.\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"7\",\"col-1\":\"Hair-stroke eyebrow micropigmentation\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"8\",\"col-1\":\"3D\\/6D eyebrow tattoo\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"9\",\"col-1\":\"Correction of another artist\'s work\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"100% of the first session price\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"11\",\"col-1\":\"Touch-up\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"400 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"13\",\"col-1\":\"Refresh within 1 year\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"80% of the original price\"}]'),
  (136, 1044, 'Price list: lip micropigmentation'),
  (138, 1044, '[{\"MIGX_id\":\"1\",\"col-1\":\"Aquarelle lip micropigmentation\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"2\",\"col-1\":\"Powder-effect lip micropigmentation\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"3\",\"col-1\":\"Ombr\\u00e9 lip micropigmentation\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"4\",\"col-1\":\"3D\\/6D lip tattoo\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"5\",\"col-1\":\"Lip contour tattoo with partial fill\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"6\",\"col-1\":\"Correction of another artist\'s work\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"100% of the first session price\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"7\",\"col-1\":\"Touch-up\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"400 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"9\",\"col-1\":\"Refresh within 1 year\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"80% of the original price\"}]'),
  (140, 1044, 'Price list: eyeliner and eyelid micropigmentation'),
  (142, 1044, '[{\"MIGX_id\":\"1\",\"col-1\":\"Eyeliner micropigmentation\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"2\",\"col-1\":\"Lash line enhancement\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"800 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"4\",\"col-1\":\"Eye contour tattoo with shading\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"5\",\"col-1\":\"Touch-up\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"400 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"6\",\"col-1\":\"Correction of another artist\'s work\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"100% of the first session price\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"7\",\"col-1\":\"Refresh within 1 year\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"80% of the original price\"}]'),
  (275, 1044, '400-600 RON');
INSERT INTO Impulse_Digital_X_site_content (`id`, `type`, `contentType`, `pagetitle`, `longtitle`, `description`, `alias`, `link_attributes`, `published`, `pub_date`, `unpub_date`, `parent`, `isfolder`, `introtext`, `content`, `richtext`, `template`, `menuindex`, `searchable`, `cacheable`, `createdby`, `createdon`, `editedby`, `editedon`, `deleted`, `deletedon`, `deletedby`, `publishedon`, `publishedby`, `menutitle`, `donthit`, `privateweb`, `privatemgr`, `content_dispo`, `hidemenu`, `class_key`, `context_key`, `content_type`, `uri`, `uri_override`, `hide_children_in_tree`, `show_in_tree`, `properties`, `alias_visible`) VALUES (1051, 'document', 'text/html', 'Powder brows micropigmentation in Bucharest', 'Powder brows micropigmentation in Bucharest, prices | LBar', 'Get powder brows micropigmentation in Bucharest at Studio LBar ⚡ Artists with 5+ years of experience ✔ Affordable prices ✎ Excellent, natural results guaranteed', 'powder-brows', '', 1, 0, 0, 1002, 0, '', '', 1, 8, 0, 1, 1, 1, UNIX_TIMESTAMP(), 1, UNIX_TIMESTAMP(), 0, 0, 0, UNIX_TIMESTAMP(), 1, 'Powder brows micropigmentation', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'modDocument', 'en', 1, 'powder-brows', 0, 0, 1, '{\"ms2gallery\":{\"media_source\":\"2\"}}', 1);
INSERT INTO Impulse_Digital_X_site_tmplvar_contentvalues (tmplvarid, contentid, value) VALUES
  (22, 1051, 'pudratcatro-min.jpg'),
  (24, 1051, 'glav3-min.jpg'),
  (26, 1051, 'Powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation may be your best option if you'),
  (27, 1051, 'Want a new look'),
  (30, 1051, 'Powder micropigmentation gives your brows a beautiful, soft outline without harsh shapes or intense colors. The delicate brow shade gives your eyes a fresh, well-groomed look.'),
  (31, 1051, 'Photo gallery – powder brows micropigmentation before and after the procedure'),
  (32, 1051, 'Price list: powder brows micropigmentation in Bucharest at LBar'),
  (34, 1051, 'Powder brows micropigmentation reviews from our lovely clients'),
  (35, 1051, 'Powder brows micropigmentation'),
  (37, 1051, '[{\"MIGX_id\":\"1\",\"questions-title\":\"Is powder brows micropigmentation painful?\",\"questions-text\":\"<p>Powder brows are considered the most painless technique, thanks to minimal skin trauma and the pigment being applied as a fine spray. An anesthetic may or may not be used during the procedure, which is why powder-effect micropigmentation is the only technique offered to pregnant women and breastfeeding new mothers.<\\/p>\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"2\",\"questions-title\":\"Who are powder brows not recommended for?\",\"questions-text\":\"<p>Powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation has no restrictions. It can be done for women of any age and with any skin type.<\\/p>\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"3\",\"questions-title\":\"What is the difference between powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation and a tattoo?\",\"questions-text\":\"<p>With a tattoo, the pigment is packed in solidly, whereas with powder brows it is applied using a powdering technique. The difference in effect is clearly visible \\u2013 powder brows look more natural and softer.<\\/p>\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"5\",\"questions-title\":\"Which is more effective: powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation or a tattoo?\",\"questions-text\":\"<p>It all depends on your preferences and goals. Powder-effect brows give a natural look and don\\u2019t require clearly defined edges. That said, the powdering acts as a base tone for your natural hairs. If you want a defined shape created by the artist, it is better to choose a tattoo in a different technique.<\\/p>\"}]'),
  (38, 1051, 'Powder brows micropigmentation in Bucharest'),
  (39, 1051, 'Gorgeous, perfectly crafted brows you won’t be able to take your eyes off'),
  (40, 1051, 'bannerpowdered2.jpg'),
  (41, 1051, '<p>Delicate work, skillfully done by a professional artist<br />Only natural shades, matched to your individual coloring<br />A painless procedure with no bleeding, no scabs and no special aftercare</p>'),
  (45, 1051, 'Powder brows micropigmentation – the most effective solution'),
  (46, 1051, '<p>How much time do you spend on your brows every day? 10 minutes? 20 minutes? We can help you get into the habit of spending that time on other important things you enjoy instead of makeup – while keeping your brows perfectly groomed. It’s that simple! Choose powder brows and you will see that you have picked the best solution for you. After all, this technique doesn’t just give you elegant, feminine brows – it transforms your whole look. You will feel more confident, and for a while you won’t need to buy any brow makeup.</p>'),
  (51, 1051, 'Want to look elegant'),
  (52, 1051, 'Semi-permanent powder-effect eyebrow tattooing is the trend of recent years. A stylish choice for those who love beauty-industry fashion and want to keep up with it.'),
  (53, 1051, 'Want to hide imperfections'),
  (54, 1051, 'Small scars and flaws, natural hairs that quickly fade in the sun – any kind of imperfection will be visually concealed and will no longer bother you.'),
  (64, 1051, '[{\"MIGX_id\":\"1\",\"col-1\":\"Powder brows micropigmentation\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min.\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"1100 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"2\",\"col-1\":\"Touch-up\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"400 RON\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"4\",\"col-1\":\"Correction of another artist\'s work\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min.\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"100% of the first session price\"},{\"MIGX_id\":\"5\",\"col-1\":\"Refresh within 1 year\",\"col-2\":\"1 hour 30 min.\",\"col-3\":\"\",\"col-4\":\"80% of the original price\"}]'),
  (65, 1051, 'Answers to frequently asked questions'),
  (66, 1051, '/en/portfolio'),
  (67, 1051, 'Why are powder brows considered the best-known technique in the world?'),
  (68, 1051, '<p>Powder brow tattooing truly is the most popular and accessible technique worldwide. This is down to how the brows look after the session: they keep their beauty and natural appearance, and at first glance it is hard to tell they have been tattooed. They look like high-quality makeup applied with eyeshadow or a pencil. The brows keep their own shape; the artist only refines them with classic, correct lines to eliminate asymmetry and give them an even look.</p>'),
  (69, 1051, '<h2>Benefits of powder brows</h2>\r\n<p>This technique suits absolutely everyone. If you want a beautiful tattoo, choose powder brows. Whatever your age, skin type or coloring, the technique is completely universal. Even on oily skin, where microblading is contraindicated, powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation looks excellent. This technique also offers the following benefits:<br />it is quick to do and long-lasting. The procedure takes no more than 1 hour 30 min, including the consultation and drawing the sketch. The effect stays visible for 1 to 2 years;<br />there is no discomfort during powder brows micropigmentation, because the pigment is placed in the upper layers of the skin;<br />allergic reactions are ruled out thanks to special mineral-based hypoallergenic pigments.<br />Powder brows save you a lot of time on daily makeup. Wherever you are and whatever you are doing, your brows will look well-groomed and gorgeous. Most importantly, this micropigmentation technique avoids the rigid shapes and intense colors that were in vogue 20 years ago. So the permanent makeup doesn’t make your eyes or face look heavy, and you don’t need to keep filling in your lashes and brows to look harmonious.</p>\r\n<h2>Stages of the powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation procedure</h2>\r\n<p>First, the artist gives you a consultation on everything you’d like to know. The pigment is selected individually based on your color type. If needed, the artist may blend two or three pigments to get the ideal shade. Next:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>The sketch is drawn. It lets the client see the brow shape and make adjustments if needed, and lets the artist strictly follow the marked boundaries and lines to keep the proportions correct.</li>\r\n<li>The procedure begins. Note that the artist does not apply an anesthetic before starting the micropigmentation. It isn’t needed, since powder brows cause minimal trauma to the skin. After the first stage, an additional anesthetic is applied to reduce pain during the rest of the pigment application and to relieve redness and swelling, which are normal skin reactions.</li>\r\n<li>The procedure is completed. The artist will give you aftercare advice and book your touch-up, which is recommended 30–45 days after the first session.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3>About the touch-up</h3>\r\n<p>To get a complete, long-lasting result with powder brows, a touch-up is a must. You can skip it, but keep in mind that:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>as the skin heals, the pigment retains a different percentage of its shade depending on your body – anywhere from 100% to 20%. The touch-up will saturate the brows with color and give them the desired shade;</li>\r\n<li>as the skin regenerates and sheds pigment, small imperfections can form and become visible. A powder brows touch-up solves this by covering minor flaws;</li>\r\n<li>the touch-up extends the effect by introducing pigment into the skin again.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>About aftercare following your micropigmentation session</h3>\r\n<p>Aftercare doesn’t require any special measures. We don’t recommend applying ointments or creams to speed up skin recovery, as we believe the skin should heal on its own. Still, for safety and to prevent infection, we recommend using chlorhexidine or a similar product for the first few days. Aftercare involves:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>avoiding direct UV exposure of your powder brows, including tanning beds. For one month, while the skin recovers, it is important to protect your brows from the sun with a hat, cap or sunglasses, or to use SPF40+ sunscreen;</li>\r\n<li>avoiding steaming the skin: no sauna, no swimming pool and no hot baths;</li>\r\n<li>washing with lukewarm water and a gentle cleanser: micellar water or a low-pH liquid soap;</li>\r\n<li>avoiding any physical contact with your brows. No scratching, massaging or trying to remove flaking skin.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The final result, and how long the tattoo stays visible, depend on how carefully you follow these recommendations.</p>\r\n<h2>Powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation – the No. 1 technique worldwide</h2>\r\n<p>Powder-effect eyebrow micropigmentation has no equal. It is the only way to get gorgeous, natural-looking brows that accentuate, rejuvenate and visually transform your face. Even dense or unruly hairs look much neater against a beautiful background. This way, you will save considerable time and money on daily brow makeup.</p>'),
  (70, 1051, '212-min.jpg'),
  (77, 1051, '/pudrovie-brovi-za-i-protiv'),
  (79, 1051, '22112021-1-min.jpg'),
  (83, 1051, '/top-7-voprosov-o-pudrovuh-brovyah'),
  (85, 1051, '22112021-2-min.jpg'),
